    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) to anchor our offensive output. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Johnson, who carries an inflated 5.15 xERA, and should see significant production if he holds the #2 spot as projected. **Jackson Merrill** is similarly positioned to exploit a soft matchup against Ritchie. While our internal mandate to chase scarcity makes us wary of his elite hold SP metrics\u2014which dock his score by 2%\u2014his dynamic platoon advantage against the right-hander makes him a must-start for today\u2019s rotation. **Andy Pages** (74.01) rounds out the top tier, providing a stable floor in the #2 hole against Rojas.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Josh Jung** (54.92) on the bench in favor of **Drake Baldwin** (58.63) and **Brayan Rocchio** (51.23). While **Josh Jung** posted a respectable score against Alcantara, the efficiency ceiling for **Drake Baldwin** was bolstered by his solid xwOBA (0.378), and we opted to prioritize the high-frequency lineup spots occupied by our MI/UTIL configuration. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** (57.05); while their projections remain strong, any shift lower in the batting order would necessitate a recalibration of their expected runs and RBI totals. The matchup against Luzardo continues to suppress the output of bench options like **Nasim Nunez** and **Curtis Mead**, who remain sidelined to preserve game caps as they battle against a challenging SP skill disadvantage.",
